    820	### C11 — D17.b: Discrete Morse on the squarefree-only divisibility Hasse diagram (NEW from S232 follow-up)
    821	**Edges/sources:** D17 closed at S232 (mode E, B-grade) with sharp
    822	identity `collapses(N) = (π(N) − π(N/2)) + Π_pow(N) + 1` for the full
    823	divisibility Hasse 1-skeleton. The squarefree-only restriction is a
    824	distinct combinatorial object: vertices are `{n ≤ N : μ(n) ≠ 0}`,
    825	covering relations are still `n | m` with `m/n` prime.
    826	**Question:** Build `H_N^{sqfree}`, run the same greedy random Morse
    827	collapse, and measure `m_0(H_N^{sqfree})`, `m_1(H_N^{sqfree})`. Does
    828	the squarefree restriction inherit the boolean lattice's known
    829	shellability such that `m_0 = polylog N`, or does it match the same
    830	linear scaling as the full lattice?
    831	**Why this is a real successor (not a duplicate of D17 closure):** the
    832	divisibility lattice on `{n ≤ N : μ(n) ≠ 0}` is *isomorphic* (as a
    833	poset) to the truncation of the boolean lattice on primes ≤ N to
    834	"subsets `S` with product `≤ N`." The boolean lattice itself has order-
    835	complex of single critical cell at the top — radically smaller `m_0`.
    836	The truncation might preserve much of this collapsibility.
    837	**A-grade target:** `m_0(H_N^{sqfree}) = O(polylog N)` would give a
    838	*polylog combinatorial encoding of `μ²(n)` (squarefree primality
    839	witness)* — first known polylog topological compression of any
    840	arithmetic indicator. Even if not directly applicable to `χ_P`, this
    841	would be a *partial-positive Correlation-Dichotomy-shaped result* on
    842	the adjacent problem of squarefree counting.
    843	**B-grade outcome:** `m_0(H_N^{sqfree})` exhibits an analogous
    844	arithmetic identity (e.g., `~ Σ_{ω(n) > c} 1`) — a refined negative-
    845	shape result orthogonal to D17.
    846	**First step:** at `N ∈ {64, 256, 1024, 4096}`, build `H_N^{sqfree}`,
    847	collect 20 random-Morse seeds, compare `m_0` to: (i) the full-lattice
    848	`H_N` (D17 baseline), (ii) ER baseline at matched `(|V|, |E|)`,
    849	(iii) `π(N) − π(N/2)`, `Σ_{ω(n)=k}` for various k.
