    1	"""
    2	D17 — Discrete Morse theory on the divisibility-poset Hasse diagram.
    3	
    4	We compute Forman's discrete-Morse critical-cell counts on the 1-skeleton
    5	of the divisibility-poset order complex on [1, N], for N in {64, 256, 1024, 4096}.
    6	
    7	Greedy random elementary collapse:
    8	  - At each step, pick a uniformly random degree-1 vertex (a "free face").
    9	  - Pair it with its unique incident edge (collapse).
    10	  - Repeat until no degree-1 vertex remains.
    11	  - Output critical-cell counts m_0 = #(remaining vertices),
    12	    m_1 = #(remaining edges).
    13	
    14	Run R seeds per N; report (min, mean, max).
    15	Compare to Erdős–Rényi G(N, |E_div|) baseline (same vertex count and edge count
    16	but uniform-random edges).
    17	
    18	Forman's Morse-Euler formula: m_0 - m_1 = chi(graph) = N - |E|.
    19	
    20	Cross-domain refs:
    21	  Forman 2002 "User's guide to discrete Morse theory" Sém. Lothar. Combin. 48
    22	  Benedetti-Lutz 2014 Exp. Math. 23, 66 (random discrete Morse)
    23	  Joswig-Pfetsch 2006 Discrete Comput. Geom. (optimal-matching NP-hardness)
    24	"""
